  "title": "Transaction Research screen to the payments ontology (illustrative)",
  "description": "Illustrative, shaped like the owner's stack: a transaction research screen in React, a Java and Spring backend that maps a GraphQL data API's types into its own DTOs, and resolvers whose SQL reads Snowflake. Written by the deep scan (web/scripts/lineage-scan.ts) from the made-up repositories in examples/lineage/; every system, file, table, column and line of code is invented. Two kinds of row: a field prov:wasDerivedFrom the field it is built from, with how (transform) and the code that does it, and a field's meaning in the ontology (skos:exactMatch, closeMatch or relatedMatch, or sssom:NoTermFound for a gap). fabric: names an ontology class's slot as the studio writes it, Class.slot.",
  "license": "https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/",
  "competency_question": "CQ-03",
  "curie_map": {
